  "summary_en": "California Assembly Bill 701, chaptered September 2021, regulates productivity quotas at large warehouse distribution centers. It requires quota disclosure, bars quotas that prevent meal/rest breaks or safety compliance, gives workers access to their work speed data, creates retaliation presumptions, and sets Labor Commissioner enforcement. It is algorithmic-monitoring-adjacent labor law, not robotics-specific.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Employers must give written descriptions of each quota on hire.",
   "Quotas cannot prevent meal/rest breaks, bathroom use, or safety-law compliance.",
   "Employees may request 90 days of their personal work speed data within 21 days.",
   "Rebuttable presumption of retaliation within 90 days of a request or complaint.",
   "Labor Commissioner enforces, with investigations triggered by injury rates 1.5 times the industry average."
  ],
